WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.488
The king's men hurried to Saint Albans, but Robin wasn't there.

2
00:00:07.489 --> 00:00:11.327
The Bishop of Hereford soon joined the king's men.

3
00:00:11.328 --> 00:00:15.202
"The king put me in charge," announced the bishop.

4
00:00:15.203 --> 00:00:19.021
He divided the men into small groups.

5
00:00:19.022 --> 00:00:22.156
They searched the countryside for Robin.

6
00:00:22.157 --> 00:00:25.284
They blocked every road and path.

7
00:00:25.285 --> 00:00:28.673
But there was no sign of Robin.

8
00:00:28.674 --> 00:00:32.977
Then the Sheriff of Nottingham and all his men joined the bishop.

9
00:00:32.978 --> 00:00:37.280
"I look forward to capturing Robin," said the sheriff.

10
00:00:37.281 --> 00:00:40.731
"So do I!" said the bishop.

11
00:00:40.732 --> 00:00:44.253
Meanwhile Robin had been walking for days.

12
00:00:44.254 --> 00:00:47.937
He whistled as he walked along the road, unworried.

13
00:00:47.938 --> 00:00:51.950
Then he paused at a stream to wash his face and get a drink of water.

14
00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:55.479
Suddenly something whizzed past his ear!

15
00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:58.252
"An arrow!" cried Robin.

16
00:00:58.253 --> 00:01:02.811
He sprang to his feet and raced through the stream and into the dense woods.

17
00:01:02.812 --> 00:01:06.829
The king's men galloped after him until they reached the woods.

18
00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:10.074
Then they left their horses and ran after him.

19
00:01:10.075 --> 00:01:14.104
But Robin knew the area much better than the king's men did.

20
00:01:14.105 --> 00:01:20.878
He crawled along the ground, and then stooped and ran, until finally he escaped the men.

21
00:01:20.879 --> 00:01:25.860
Panting, he finally stopped at the top of a hill.

22
00:01:25.861 --> 00:01:29.233
Below he saw even more of the king's men.

23
00:01:29.234 --> 00:01:35.039
"I need a disguise!" Robin's stomach growled. "And some food!"

24
00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:39.312
Robin was careful to stay hidden as he walked toward Nottingham.

25
00:01:39.313 --> 00:01:43.291
He soon spotted a shoemaker.

26
00:01:43.292 --> 00:01:45.736
"Hello, there!" Robin called.

27
00:01:45.737 --> 00:01:47.723
"I was admiring your outfit.

28
00:01:47.724 --> 00:01:49.610
Will you change clothes with me?

29
00:01:49.611 --> 00:01:51.358
And share your lunch?"

30
00:01:51.359 --> 00:01:52.962
The shoemaker laughed.

31
00:01:52.963 --> 00:01:56.680
"Your clothes are much nicer than mine.

32
00:01:56.681 --> 00:01:59.762
Why do you want to change?"

33
00:01:59.763 --> 00:02:03.948
"I'm playing a joke on someone." Robin held out his hand.

34
00:02:03.949 --> 00:02:07.057
"Here, I'll give you ten gold coins."

35
00:02:07.058 --> 00:02:09.406
"All right!"

36
00:02:09.407 --> 00:02:12.908
The two men changed clothes and sat down to eat.

37
00:02:12.909 --> 00:02:18.178
They were exchanging stories when the king's men suddenly interrupted them.

38
00:02:18.179 --> 00:02:21.051
"There he is!" one of the men called.

39
00:02:21.052 --> 00:02:25.221
"Robin Hood, you're under arrest!" said another man to the shoemaker.

40
00:02:25.222 --> 00:02:28.493
"I'm not Robin Hood!" said the shoemaker.

41
00:02:28.494 --> 00:02:31.611
But the king's men didn't listen to the shoemaker.

42
00:02:31.612 --> 00:02:36.127
They tied his hands behind him and then took him away.

43
00:02:36.128 --> 00:02:38.887
Robin knew the shoemaker would be all right.

44
00:02:38.888 --> 00:02:43.603
The bishop would quickly realize the shoemaker wasn't Robin.

45
00:02:43.604 --> 00:02:45.692
So Robin continued walking.

46
00:02:45.693 --> 00:02:48.603
But by dark, he was exhausted.

47
00:02:48.604 --> 00:02:52.186
"I'd better get some sleep," Robin thought.

48
00:02:52.187 --> 00:02:57.347
He stopped at the next inn along the road and got one of the last available beds.

49
00:02:57.348 --> 00:03:02.046
He fell asleep almost before his head touched the pillow.

50
00:03:02.047 --> 00:03:06.824
When Robin awoke at dawn, he found a friar sleeping in the next bed.

51
00:03:06.825 --> 00:03:09.724
Quickly he dressed in the friar's clothes.

52
00:03:09.725 --> 00:03:13.291
Outside he took the friar's mule and hurried away.

53
00:03:13.292 --> 00:03:18.684
Disguised as a friar, Robin passed right by some of the king's men.

54
00:03:18.685 --> 00:03:23.486
As Robin rode down a lane, he spotted a familiar knight.

55
00:03:23.487 --> 00:03:29.861
"Sir Richard, how nice to see you!" exclaimed Robin, leaping off the mule.

56
00:03:29.862 --> 00:03:34.918
"I've been on the run." He told Sir Richard about the men chasing him.

57
00:03:34.919 --> 00:03:39.436
"But I'll soon be safely back in Sherwood Forest."

58
00:03:39.437 --> 00:03:41.564
Sir Richard shook his head.

59
00:03:41.565 --> 00:03:43.691
"You're in great danger, Robin.

60
00:03:43.692 --> 00:03:46.270
Everyone knows you're disguised as a friar.

61
00:03:46.271 --> 00:03:47.765
There's only one thing to do.

62
00:03:47.766 --> 00:03:50.985
Go back to London and ask for Queen Eleanor's help."

63
00:03:50.986 --> 00:03:55.617
"Back to London?" Robin felt his heart sink.

64
00:03:55.618 --> 00:03:58.300
"Yes, come with me," Sir Richard said.

65
00:03:58.301 --> 00:04:00.162
"You can dress as one of my men.

66
00:04:00.163 --> 00:04:02.738
We'll travel with you to London."

67
00:04:02.739 --> 00:04:08.206
Robin didn't want to go back to London, but Sir Richard was a very wise knight.

68
00:04:08.207 --> 00:04:13.803
So Robin changed his clothes once again and followed Sir Richard.

69
00:04:13.804 --> 00:04:19.112
Queen Eleanor was walking in her garden among the roses when a man leaped over the wall.

70
00:04:19.113 --> 00:04:23.482
He hung onto the wall for a moment before dropping lightly on the grass.

71
00:04:23.483 --> 00:04:28.167
Her maids shrieked, but the queen recognized Robin.

72
00:04:28.168 --> 00:04:32.067
"Your Majesty!" Robin knelt at her feet.

73
00:04:32.068 --> 00:04:35.000
"Help! The king's men are after me."

74
00:04:35.001 --> 00:04:38.453
"What?" The queen looked furious.

75
00:04:38.454 --> 00:04:41.534
"The king has broken his promise.

76
00:04:41.535 --> 00:04:46.910
He won't get away with this! Wait here, Robin."

77
00:04:46.911 --> 00:04:49.113
Queen Eleanor returned soon.

78
00:04:49.114 --> 00:04:52.321
"You can travel safely, Robin.

79
00:04:52.322 --> 00:04:56.496
The king has promised me again that you will be safe."

80
00:04:56.497 --> 00:05:00.058
Robin saw that her eyes were still bright with anger.

81
00:05:00.059 --> 00:05:05.143
"And this time he will not break his promise!"

82
00:05:05.144 --> 00:05:09.039
After three days Robin set off for home again.

83
00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:17.382
Along the way he passed many of the king's men, but this time no one dared to harm him.

84
00:05:17.383 --> 00:05:25.698
At last Robin arrived safely back in Sherwood Forest.

85
00:05:25.699 --> 00:05:34.233
And there he stayed for many years with his merry men, singing, feasting, and shooting his bow and arrow.

